{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:11f38b98df048679","name":"5-BT Threat Analysis Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-11f38b98df048679","title":"5-BT Threat Analysis Droid","revision":21137,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:13:36Z","sha256":"4483f26054d345fba6ede0e903cdfddff2c10a752c42e7f4f809ec57a248921c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21137","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=5-BT%20Threat%20Analysis%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-11f38b98df048679","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Built by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arakyd Industries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arakyd_Industries","referenceId":"reference:53475569f2ae9d67"}," decades before some of its more notorious Droids, the 5-BT Threat Analysis Droid is the precursor to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mark VII \"Inquisitor\" Seeker Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_VII_%22Inquisitor%22_Seeker_Droid","referenceId":"reference:ed245c267142cec1"}," and to other notorious models. The 5-BT is a tiny spherical Droid designed to accompany a VIP during assignments. A wide array of sensors scan for threats to its owner, including poisoned food or drink, eavesdropping devices, or hidden assassins. In addition, the 5-BT monitors a person's voice and nonverbal cues to detect stress- possibly indicating an impending attack- and dishonesty. New 5-BTs are sold with a bracelet that enables the Droid to warn its owner of a threat by sending a signal that causes the bracelet to vibrate discreetly. Alternatively, the Droid's warning can be directed to an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Earbud Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Earbud_Comlink","referenceId":"reference:ef68567404526815"},". The 5-BT is also equipped with the equivalent of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hold-Out Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hold-Out_Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:99ddc9f0285574f3"},", providing additional protection of its owner when warnings alone are insufficient.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["5-BT Threat Analysis Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["5-BT Threat Analysis Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Tiny ",{"tag":"a","children":["1st-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/1st-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +13; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 1 Unassigned; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Translator Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Translator_Unit","referenceId":"reference:0bcd4b383b11cac0"}," (DC 10)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.mirah